# Either the owner or the approver bot reviews a change by default. The bot approves only
# after the one non-Claude review passes, CI is green and a run-proof is present (decisions
# ledger 2026-11-04). The owner-only block at the end keeps the gate, the checks and the
# reserved classes his: GitHub's Actions hardening guide says to code-own workflow files,
# and its code owners docs say to own this file. Last match wins.
*                           @nish3451 @nishfleet-approver

# No owner, so these merge on the required checks alone: docs, lockfiles and pure
# formatting config. Dependabot's npm patch and minor updates touch only lockfiles
# (versioning-strategy: increase-if-necessary in dependabot.yml), so GitHub's
# auto-merge recipe still merges them. Majors and manifest edits wait for the owner.
/docs/
/*.md
**/package-lock.json
/go.sum
/.editorconfig
/.prettierrc.json
/.prettierignore
/.git-blame-ignore-revs

